        "title": "fix: harden subprocess, maintenance, and output paths",
        "body": "Related: #100407, #100406, #100410, #100393, #100390, #100380, #100337, #100327, #100302, #100028\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes ten small reliability defects where child-stream errors could crash long-running processes, background sweeps could abort or retain stale state, diagnostics hid actionable failures, model output cleanup could lose visible content, and Android audio capture could spin after device loss.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis maintainer takeover keeps the contributor reports and regression coverage while moving fixes to their shared owners: the Android recorder covers both capture consumers, approval errors retain request/wait phase, remote refresh clears stale eligibility, ANSI cleanup preserves incomplete chunks, and standalone parameter cleanup runs only after fail-closed tool-call stripping. The unrelated transcript partial-read proposal from #100404 was excluded because swallowing shared reader errors could corrupt integrity-sensitive append decisions; #100410 supplies the tenth qualified fix.\n\n## User Impact\n\nExec and TUI subprocesses no longer crash on independent output-pipe faults; remote skill and subagent maintenance survives isolated failures; users receive accurate skill and approval diagnostics; terminal/model output remains readable without control injection; and Android transcription and Talk sessions stop cleanly when an input device disappears.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Structured autoreview: clean, no actionable findings after accepted fixes.\n- Targeted Oxfmt and Oxlint: clean on all changed TypeScript files.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n- Sanitized AWS Crabbox `run_7be50f178fb6` on exact head `ff6af222600a88ec1a0fc902b38ea2c5d00b5b48`: 347 focused tests passed across six Vitest shards.\n- Sanitized AWS Crabbox `run_b18909b055e4`: Android Play and third-party `AndroidAudioInputSessionTest` variants passed on JDK 17 / SDK 36 (61 Gradle tasks).\n- Sanitized AWS Crabbox `run_b127a1d33ccb`: `pnpm check:changed` passed, including core/test typechecks, all core lint shards, and architecture guards.\n- Isolation proof: AWS lease `cbx_d6eda2d776b1`, public network, no Tailscale, no instance profile, no credential hydration, `CRABBOX_ENV_ALLOW=CI`.\n\nContributor provenance is preserved in each focused commit and the changelog.\n",
